Founded in 1898, Peking University (PKU) stands as the first national university in China's modern history. The university is organized into seven faculties: Humanities, Social Sciences, Sciences, Health Sciences, Economics and Management, Engineering, and Information Science and Technology. PKU comprises 55 colleges and departments, offering 137 undergraduate programs, 286 master's programs, and 263 doctoral programs. While maintaining a strong foundation in fundamental sciences, the university has also dedicated significant focus to the development of applied sciences.
PKU is distinguished by its exceptional research infrastructure and a highly accomplished faculty known for their broad research interests and deep expertise. The university employs 3,821 full-time academic staff, including 1,730 professors and 1,658 associate professors. PKU hosts 14 national key laboratories, 5 national engineering research centers, and 6 affiliated hospitals and medical centers.
The Peking University Library, the largest university library in Asia, holds a collection of 8.718 million volumes alongside extensive Chinese and foreign periodicals and newspapers. It also serves as a comprehensive modern information center.
International students can pursue the following study options at PKU:
(1) Undergraduate or graduate degree programs;
(2) Non-degree visiting student programs;
(3) Foundation (Pre-university) programs;
(4) Short-term language courses or Chinese studies programs.

Hainan Normal University is a higher education institution jointly established by the Hainan Provincial People’s Government and the Ministry of Education. As a key provincial university, it serves as a major training base and scientific research center in Hainan for outstanding teachers and high-level specialized professionals.
The university actively expands its international cooperation and exchanges. It has established inter-institutional partnerships with more than 110 universities and educational organizations in over 20 countries, promoting active academic collaboration.
Among its international cooperative programs, Hainan Normal University offers:
A joint undergraduate program in Radio and Television Directing with St. Petersburg State University of Film and Television (Russia);
A joint undergraduate program in Preschool Education with DePaul University (USA);
A joint undergraduate program in Environmental Design with Rome University of Fine Arts (RUFA) (Italy);
A collaboratively built Software Engineering program with NIIT (National Institute of Information Technology) of India;
And jointly established the Confucius Institute at SEGi University with SEGi University (Malaysia).
In addition, the university has launched several joint graduate (master’s and doctoral) training programs with overseas institutions such as The University of Texas at Arlington (USA), Saint Peter’s University (USA), and Rome University of Fine Arts (RUFA) (Italy).
Domestically, Hainan Normal University has signed a counterpart support agreement with Shaanxi Normal University and entered into a new-round cooperation agreement with Southwest University.
